{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "iterative",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 8, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.1,
      "why": "Low area but serial (1 micro-rotation/cycle). To meet the 32-request burst within 0.44 us, it would need Fmax >= 72.7*(N+3) MHz; for N>=12 (needed for 2^-12 accuracy) this exceeds 1 GHz, likely infeasible on Artix-7. Small budget to confirm infeasibility and catch any edge case with very high Fmax and low N."
    },
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 12, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 4, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]},
        {"param": "k", "low": 3, "high": 8, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 0.9,
      "why": "Processes k micro-rotations/cycle, reducing cycles/result to ceil(N/k)+3. With k=8 and N=12..16, cycles/result is 5..6, requiring Fmax ~360..440 MHz, which is plausible on Artix-7. Main family to map the feasible Pareto front of area vs accuracy under the batch constraint. Ranges cover the accuracy boundary (N~12-16, W~14-16) and throughput boundary (k~4-8)."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec's system constraint (32 requests within 0.44 us of a 1 MHz tick) demands very high instantaneous throughput. iterative cannot plausibly meet this because its serial nature forces Fmax >= 72.7*(N+3) MHz, which for N>=12 (needed for 2^-12 accuracy) exceeds 1 GHz. unrolled_k can meet it by processing k micro-rotations per cycle, trading area for throughput. We allocate 10% of the budget to iterative to confirm infeasibility and 90% to unrolled_k to map the Pareto front over k, N, and data_width, focusing on the feasible region where accuracy_bits >= 12 and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44."
}

{ "decision": "add_family",
  "next_plan": {
    "families": [
      {
        "budget_share": 0.6,
        "family": "pipelined",
        "ranges": [
          { "choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 14, "param": "data_width" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 16, "low": 10, "param": "n_iter" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "angle_guard" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard" }
        ]
      ,
      "why": "1 result/cycle: throughput_msps = fmax, the only way past the 32 MSPS wall; latency N+2 keeps the 32-request batch inside 0.44 us" }
      ,
      {
        "budget_share": 0.4,
        "family": "pipelined_m",
        "ranges": [
          { "choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": null, "low": null, "param": "rounding" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 20, "low": 14, "param": "data_width" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 16, "low": 10, "param": "n_iter" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "angle_guard" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard" },
          { "choices": null, "high": 4, "low": 2, "param": "m" }
        ]
      ,
      "why": "same 1 result/cycle with fewer pipeline registers (lower LUTs+FFs, the objective) and shorter latency; m trades Fmax against area but can cut the batch tail" }
    ]
  ,
  "rationale": "The front is empty and the failure pattern is unambiguous. Accuracy is already solved: the best design seen reaches 2^-16.57 (constraint is 2^-12), and rule says accuracy depends only on data_width/n_iter/angle_guard/frac_guard/rounding, i.e. it is family-independent. The two binding constraints are throughput_msps >= 32 (100% violate, best 17.2 MSPS) and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44 (100% violate, best 1.85 us) - both are rate constraints. iterative and unrolled_k are inherently multi-cycle-per-result families: their best observed throughputs (17.2 and 14.0 MSPS) are far below 32 and their N+3 / ceil(N/k)+3 result intervals make a 32-request burst take ~1.9-2.9 us. No amount of parameter refinement inside those families can close a 2x rate gap, so refine/widen are wasted budget. pipelined and pipelined_m emit 1 result/cycle, so throughput_msps = fmax (Artix-7 CORDIC pipelines clear 32 MSPS comfortably), and a 32-deep burst completes in roughly (N+2)+31 cycles - at ~100 MHz with N~12-16 that is ~0.33-0.49 us, which is why I pin n_iter to 10..16 so the batch tail fits the 0.44 us window. Budget: 40 evals left, ~24 to pipelined and ~16 to pipelined_m, data_width 14..20 to hold accuracy well above 12 bits without paying area, and m 2..4 to probe the Fmax/register-count trade that directly drives the luts_plus_ffs objective." } 
  ,
  "rationale": "Accuracy is not the blocker (best 2^-16.57 vs required 2^-12, and it is family-independent); the blockers are throughput_msps >= 32 (best 17.2) and sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44 (best 1.85 us), both rate constraints unreachable in the multi-cycle iterative/unrolled_k families. Only the pipelined families deliver 1 result/cycle." }

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "next_plan": null,
  "rationale": "Budget exhausted (100/100 evals, final round) and no feasible design found: 0/100 evaluations satisfy the constraints. The hard blockers are throughput and burst latency: best throughput seen is 22 MSPS (iterative) vs the required 32 MSPS, and best sys_p99_batch_us is 1.45 us vs the required 0.44 us. Accuracy is not the blocker — best max_abs_err is 3.12e-08 (2^-24.93), far below the 2^-12 limit. The explored families (iterative, unrolled_k) top out well below 32 MSPS and their 32-request batch times are ~1.45 us, >0.44 us. Pipelined/pipelined_m would be the natural families to test for 1 result/cycle, but no evaluation budget remains, so I stop rather than claim the entire registry is infeasible."
}
